I’ll look for human longitudinal or intervention studies measuring DNA double-strand-break markers in mononuclear cells before and after smoking cessation, then assess the direction and strength of the evidence and record the key finding.

Tool call: go_search_agent
Tool call input: {'knowledge_bases': ['pubmed_papers'], 'search_rounds_budget': 3, 'search_target': 'Determine whether smoking cessation reverses DNA double-strand breaks in human peripheral blood mononuclear cells/mononuclear leukocytes. Find longitudinal human cessation studies measuring DSBs or validated DSB markers (e.g., γH2AX, comet assay) before and after cessation, report population, timing, results, and any limits. Distinguish repair/reversal from reduced ongoing damage.'}

Plan:
1. [✓] Locate a direct human smoking-cessation study on mononuclear-cell DSBs (PMID: 25093845).
2. [ ] Verify the study’s methods, follow-up and results from its PubMed record, and distinguish a measured decline in DSB burden from proof that individual breaks were repaired.
3. [ ] Record the evidence and give a calibrated yes/no conclusion.

A direct-match 2014 paper has surfaced, with a title that states reversal. I’ll retrieve its abstract and publication details to confirm what was actually measured and how strongly it supports that wording.

Tool call: code_execution
Tool call input: {'code': "import requests, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
u='https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi'
r=requests.get(u,params={'db':'pubmed','id':'25093845','rettype':'abstract','retmode':'xml'},timeout=20)
print('HTTP',r.status_code)
root=ET.fromstring(r.text)
for el in root.findall('.//ArticleTitle'): print('TITLE:', ''.join(el.itertext()))
for el in root.findall('.//Abstract/AbstractText'): print('ABSTRACT:',el.get('Label',''), ''.join(el.itertext()))
for el in root.findall('.//Journal/Title'): print('JOURNAL:',el.text)
for el in root.findall('.//PubDate'): print('PUBDATE:', ' '.join(x.text or '' for x in el))
for el in root.findall('.//Author'): print('',end='')
print('PMID: 25093845')", 'language': 'python'}
